cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Ecohydrological Response Units (UREH) in the Cuitzmala River Basin"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Islas"
    given-names: "Luis Alfredo"

repository-code: "https://github.com/L-Islas/ureh-cuitzmala"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - ecohydrology
  - hydrological regionalization
  - Bayesian networks
  - Ecohydrological Response Units
  - UREH
  - watershed
  - Cuitzmala River Basin
  - hydrological function
  - Gower distance
  - PAM clustering

abstract: >-
  Reproducible code, analysis-ready data, Bayesian-network model
  specification, numerical outputs, spatial results, and manuscript
  figures supporting an ecohydrological regionalization of the
  Cuitzmala River Basin, Jalisco, Mexico. The workflow integrates
  local biophysical attributes, hydrological processes, and upstream
  water contribution to derive Ecohydrological Response Units (UREH),
  evaluate their sensitivity to controlled changes in evidence, and
  examine their correspondence with a multivariate similarity-based
  regionalization.